WEBVTT

1
00:00:15.599 --> 00:00:16.739
Sawyer smiled at me.

2
00:00:16.759 --> 00:00:18.900
"Yes, Huck," he said.

3
00:00:18.920 --> 00:00:20.701
"Of course I'll help you."

4
00:00:21.802 --> 00:00:23.883
He was quiet for a few minutes thinking.

5
00:00:25.024 --> 00:00:29.346
Then he grinned and told me how I could keep pretending to be Tom Sawyer.

6
00:00:30.367 --> 00:00:31.948
I thought his plan just might work.

7
00:00:32.624 --> 00:00:35.766
I never knew anyone better at thinking up plans than Tom.

8
00:00:37.747 --> 00:00:39.788
Soon we were back at the Phelps' house.

9
00:00:40.728 --> 00:00:42.449
"Well, who's this?"

10
00:00:43.330 --> 00:00:45.411
Aunt Sally asked when we came in the door.

11
00:00:46.311 --> 00:00:49.593
All the little cousins gathered around, looking at us curiously.

12
00:00:49.613 --> 00:00:52.675
"This is my brother, Sid," I said.

13
00:00:52.695 --> 00:00:55.276
"I wanted his visit to be a surprise.

14
00:00:56.017 --> 00:00:58.978
That's why I had to go back to the dock—to get him and bring him here."

15
00:01:00.439 --> 00:01:02.300
Aunt Sally looked really surprised.

16
00:01:03.448 --> 00:01:10.170
"We're certainly happy to see you," she said, "but my sister's letter said only Tom would be visiting."

17
00:01:10.190 --> 00:01:13.531
"That's right," said the real Tom.

18
00:01:13.551 --> 00:01:19.773
"But I begged and begged Aunt Polly to let me come, and at the last minute she finally

19
00:01:19.833 --> 00:01:21.833
agreed. So here I am!"

20
00:01:23.134 --> 00:01:25.014
Aunt Sally gave him a big hug.

21
00:01:26.114 --> 00:01:28.935
Then she called Uncle Silas to come and meet Sid.

22
00:01:29.936 --> 00:01:34.437
They were nice people, and it never occurred to them that they were being tricked.

23
00:01:35.617 --> 00:01:40.058
The Phelpses fed us a delicious dinner with enough food for seven families.

24
00:01:41.819 --> 00:01:47.060
Tom and I had agreed that we must not ask about Jim because we weren't supposed to know

25
00:01:47.100 --> 00:01:47.480
about him.

26
00:01:48.401 --> 00:01:50.361
But we hoped that someone would mention him.

27
00:01:51.342 --> 00:01:53.202
Finally, during dinner, someone did.

28
00:01:54.242 --> 00:01:59.704
One of my little cousins asked, "Pa, may Tom and Sid and I go to the show in

29
00:01:59.744 --> 00:02:03.345
town?" "No," said Uncle Silas.

30
00:02:04.406 --> 00:02:07.268
"I heard from the runaway slave that it is a stupid show.

31
00:02:08.249 --> 00:02:11.611
He said those two actors have been cheating people all along the river.

32
00:02:12.832 --> 00:02:17.215
I warned a man in town, and he said the townspeople would capture the rascals this evening and

33
00:02:17.275 --> 00:02:18.256
throw them out of town."

34
00:02:19.677 --> 00:02:22.378
Now Tom and I knew that Jim really was nearby.

35
00:02:23.239 --> 00:02:27.422
I said that my brother and I were tired, and we went up to our bedroom right after

36
00:02:27.462 --> 00:02:31.441
dinner. "I've got to warn the king and the duke," I told Tom.

37
00:02:31.461 --> 00:02:33.563
"They don't know that they're in danger."

38
00:02:35.264 --> 00:02:40.268
We climbed out of our bedroom window and slid down the lightning rod that ran up the side

39
00:02:40.288 --> 00:02:40.769
of the house.

40
00:02:41.869 --> 00:02:47.294
We ran down the road, but when we reached the town, we met a noisy, angry crowd.

41
00:02:48.315 --> 00:02:53.619
Some of them were carrying a long pole, with two fellows tied up and hanging underneath it.

42
00:02:55.000 --> 00:02:59.024
It was hard to recognize them, but I knew they must be the king and the duke.

43
00:02:59.984 --> 00:03:04.207
Even though they were scoundrels, I felt sad to see them being treated so roughly.

44
00:03:05.388 --> 00:03:09.230
Tom and I saw that we couldn't do anything to help, so we turned back.

45
00:03:10.311 --> 00:03:13.834
At first we were quiet, thinking about the two men as we walked.

46
00:03:14.614 --> 00:03:17.676
Then Tom said, "I think I know where Jim is!"

47
00:03:17.696 --> 00:03:19.998
"Where?" I asked.

48
00:03:20.018 --> 00:03:22.639
"In that shed behind the kitchen.

49
00:03:23.680 --> 00:03:26.762
Didn't you see the servant go out the back door while we were eating?

50
00:03:27.723 --> 00:03:29.084
He was carrying some food.

51
00:03:29.652 --> 00:03:30.933
Who do you think it was for?"

52
00:03:30.953 --> 00:03:34.435
"I don't know," I said.

53
00:03:34.455 --> 00:03:35.936
"Maybe for the dogs?"

54
00:03:37.436 --> 00:03:41.198
"No, he must be locked in the shed," Tom continued.

55
00:03:41.219 --> 00:03:47.722
"When we were getting up from the table, the servant brought Uncle Silas a big key, and he

56
00:03:47.762 --> 00:03:48.783
put it in his pocket."

57
00:03:50.384 --> 00:03:52.585
I couldn't believe how smart Tom was.

58
00:03:53.005 --> 00:03:54.486
He had figured out everything.

59
00:03:54.506 --> 00:03:56.987
"So how should we rescue Jim?"

60
00:03:57.568 --> 00:03:58.108
Tom asked.

61
00:03:59.136 --> 00:04:03.198
"Let's find out from the servant whether Jim is really in the shed," I said.

62
00:04:03.218 --> 00:04:08.381
"Then, tomorrow night, when Uncle Silas is asleep, we'll take the key from his pocket.

63
00:04:09.422 --> 00:04:12.183
He leaves his trousers hanging on the chair in his bedroom.

64
00:04:12.944 --> 00:04:16.225
We'll free Jim and run down to the riverbank where the raft is hidden.

65
00:04:17.406 --> 00:04:19.147
We'll all get aboard and escape down the river.

66
00:04:20.348 --> 00:04:21.008
Wouldn't that work?"

67
00:04:22.829 --> 00:04:26.751
"It might work," said Tom, looking very disappointed.

68
00:04:28.492 --> 00:04:29.753
"But it's too simple."

69
00:04:30.933 --> 00:04:35.715
Then Tom told me his plan, which had lots of things to do and would take quite a

70
00:04:35.775 --> 00:04:41.458
while. I thought his plan would probably free Jim, but it might also get us killed.

71
00:04:43.158 --> 00:04:47.160
However, I was so grateful to him for helping me that I didn't object.

72
00:04:48.121 --> 00:04:52.903
When we got back, the house was dark and still, so we tiptoed around to the shed.

73
00:04:54.023 --> 00:04:59.307
On the back wall of the shed, we saw a high square window with a board nailed across

74
00:04:59.367 --> 00:05:04.870
it. "We can pull off that board," I said, "and then Jim can squeeze out the window."

75
00:05:06.532 --> 00:05:09.654
"I hope we can think of an escape that's more interesting than that!"

76
00:05:10.294 --> 00:05:11.475
said Tom scornfully.

77
00:05:12.736 --> 00:05:15.378
Next to the shed was a small unlocked hut.

78
00:05:16.418 --> 00:05:19.621
We opened the door, struck a match, and looked inside.

79
00:05:20.481 --> 00:05:24.244
We saw rusty old tools, including spades and picks.

80
00:05:25.464 --> 00:05:28.946
"Now I know what we can do," said Tom happily.

81
00:05:28.966 --> 00:05:31.508
"We can dig Jim out.

82
00:05:31.968 --> 00:05:33.509
It will only take about a week."

83
00:05:36.230 --> 00:05:41.513
The back door of the house wasn't locked, so I entered quietly and went up to the bedroom.

84
00:05:42.474 --> 00:05:48.958
But Tom, who always wanted adventures, was determined to climb up the lightning rod and through the window.

85
00:05:50.839 --> 00:05:55.966
After he slipped and fell three times, I finally persuaded him to use the stairs like me.
